I'm building a Dash (Plotly) app deployed on Databricks Apps, styled with Dash Bootstrap Components (dbc). The app connects to a Databricks Genie Space for natural language querying of policy data.

I need you to build a full-page investigation dashboard UI for actuaries to diagnose why scoring model drivers are unscored. Here is the complete spec:

---

## LAYOUT

Use dbc.Container(fluid=True) with a fixed-height viewport. The layout has 3 columns:
- Left sidebar: 2 cols wide (filters)
- Center panel: 7 cols wide (KPIs + reason cards + driver table)
- Right panel: 3 cols wide (Genie chat)

Use a top navbar built with dbc.Navbar containing:
- Brand name "PolicyIQ" with a teal dot (●) prefix
- Nav tabs: Overview | Driver investigation (active) | Portfolio | Mortality
- Right-aligned status badge: green dot + "Genie · Databricks"

---

## LEFT SIDEBAR

Wrap in a dbc.Card with no border-radius on the right side, full height, light background.

Include these filter sections, each with a small uppercase label:

1. Text search input (dbc.Input) — placeholder: "e.g. POL-00291, age_band…"

2. Source table — dbc.Checklist as pills:
   options: ["Policy table", "Client table", "Both / join issue"]
   all checked by default

3. Unscored reason category — dbc.Checklist as pills:
   options: ["Missing value", "Out of range", "Mapping error", "Join failure", "Inactive policy", "Future effective"]
   first 4 checked by default

4. Driver / feature — dbc.Checklist as pills:
   options: ["age_band", "smoker_status", "gender", "face_amount", "duration", "underwriting_class", "province", "product_code"]
   first 3 checked by default

5. Severity — dbc.Checklist as pills:
   options: ["High", "Med", "Low"]
   style each pill with its semantic color (High=red, Med=amber, Low=green)

At the bottom: snapshot label showing "2024-Q4 · 1.2M policies" and "Last refresh: 2h ago"

---

## CENTER PANEL — TOP: KPI ROW

4 dbc.Card metric cards in a dbc.Row, each showing:
1. "Total drivers" → 24, subtitle "in scoring model"
2. "Unscored drivers" → 7 (red), subtitle "29% of model"
3. "Policies affected" → 41.3K, subtitle "4.9% of portfolio"
4. "Est. score impact" → –8.2% (amber), subtitle "avg score degradation"

---

## CENTER PANEL — MIDDLE: REASON BREAKDOWN CARDS

A 2x2 grid of dbc.Card components (dbc.Row with 2 dbc.Col each).
Each card is clickable and updates a dcc.Store called "active-reason-store".
The active card gets a colored left border accent (2px).

Card 1 — Missing value
- Source badge: "Policy + Client" (amber pill)
- Count: 18,240
- Subtitle: "drivers with null / blank fields"
- A small plotly bar chart (go.Bar) showing weekly trend, purple bars
- id: "card-missing"

Card 2 — Out of range
- Source badge: "Policy table" (purple pill)
- Count: 10,482
- Subtitle: "values outside model bounds"
- Small bar chart, coral/red bars
- id: "card-oor"

Card 3 — Join failure
- Source badge: "Policy + Client" (amber pill)
- Count: 7,901
- Subtitle: "client_id not matched to policy"
- Small bar chart, teal bars
- id: "card-join"

Card 4 — Mapping error
- Source badge: "Client table" (teal pill)
- Count: 4,620
- Subtitle: "unrecognised category codes"
- Small bar chart, amber bars
- id: "card-mapping"

Each card has an n_clicks property. Wire a callback that:
- Sets the active-reason-store value to the clicked reason name
- Adds a CSS class "active-card" to the clicked card (left border accent)
- Updates the Genie chat context banner with the selected reason

---

## CENTER PANEL — BOTTOM: DRIVER DETAIL TABLE

Use dash_table.DataTable with id="driver-table".

Columns:
- Driver (string)
- Source (string) — render as colored pill using style_data_conditional
- Reason (string) — colored pill
- Severity (string) — colored pill
- Affected (integer, formatted with comma separator)
- Coverage % (float, show as a progress bar using style_data_conditional background trick)

Data (hardcode as default, will be replaced by Genie callback):
[
  {"driver": "smoker_status", "source": "Client", "reason": "Missing", "severity": "High", "affected": 12401, "coverage": 30},
  {"driver": "age_band", "source": "Policy", "reason": "Out of range", "severity": "High", "affected": 9820, "coverage": 24},
  {"driver": "client_id (join)", "source": "Both", "reason": "Join failure", "severity": "Med", "affected": 7901, "coverage": 19},
  {"driver": "underwriting_class", "source": "Client", "reason": "Mapping error", "severity": "Med", "affected": 4620, "coverage": 11},
  {"driver": "gender", "source": "Client", "reason": "Missing", "severity": "Low", "affected": 3210, "coverage": 8},
  {"driver": "face_amount", "source": "Policy", "reason": "Out of range", "severity": "Med", "affected": 2840, "coverage": 7},
  {"driver": "province", "source": "Policy", "reason": "Mapping error", "severity": "Low", "affected": 510, "coverage": 1}
]

Style rules via style_data_conditional:
- Source "Client" → purple pill background #EEEDFE, text #3C3489
- Source "Policy" → teal pill background #E1F5EE, text #085041
- Source "Both" → amber pill background #FAEEDA, text #633806
- Severity "High" → red text #A32D2D
- Severity "Med" → amber text #854F0B
- Severity "Low" → green text #3B6D11
- Coverage column: use linear-gradient background trick to simulate a progress bar

Sort by "affected" descending by default. Enable sort_action="native".

Wire a callback: when active-reason-store changes OR sidebar filters change, filter the table rows accordingly.

---

## RIGHT PANEL — GENIE CHAT

Build a chat interface in a full-height dbc.Card. Structure:

1. Card header: "Investigate with Genie" title + "SQL · Genie" purple pill badge

2. Context banner (dbc.Alert, id="context-banner", color="primary", light=True):
   Shows "Active context: [reason] · [driver] · [N] records"
   Updates via callback when active-reason-store changes

3. Chat message area: a scrollable div (id="chat-messages") containing dbc.Card bubbles.
   User messages: right-aligned, light gray background
   AI messages: left-aligned, light teal background #E1F5EE, teal border

4. Suggested prompts — 3 dbc.Button components (outline, small, full width):
   - "Fix rate if we backfill smoker_status ↗"
   - "Broker channels with most missing drivers ↗"
   - "Score uplift if all drivers fixed ↗"
   Clicking a suggested prompt populates the input and triggers send.

5. Input row: dbc.Input (id="chat-input", placeholder="Dig deeper into any driver or cohort…") + dbc.Button("Send", id="send-btn")

---

## GENIE SPACE CALLBACK

Create a callback with:
- Input: send-btn n_clicks, chat-input value, active-reason-store data
- State: chat-messages children (for conversation history)
- Output: chat-messages children (append new bubbles), chat-input value (clear after send)

Inside the callback, call the Databricks Genie Space API:
- Use the existing DATABRICKS_HOST and GENIE_SPACE_ID environment variables
- Endpoint: POST {DATABRICKS_HOST}/api/2.0/genie/spaces/{GENIE_SPACE_ID}/start-conversation
- Auth: Bearer token from environment variable DATABRICKS_TOKEN
- Pass the user message as the query, prepend the active context (reason + driver filters) to the message for grounding
- Parse the response and append an AI message bubble
- Handle errors gracefully with a dbc.Alert danger bubble

---

## STYLING

Create an external stylesheet or inline styles using these rules:
- Font: system-ui, sans-serif
- Background: #F8F8F6 (page), #FFFFFF (cards)
- All cards: border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08), border-radius: 8px
- Active reason card: border-left: 3px solid #7F77DD
- KPI values: font-size: 22px, font-weight: 500
- Sidebar filter pills: small rounded buttons, toggle on/off with n_clicks, use dbc.Button with outline style
- Table: no cell borders, alternating row background, sticky header
- Navbar: white background, bottom border 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08), no box-shadow
- Chat bubbles: border-radius: 10px, max-width: 90%, padding: 8px 12px

---

## FILE STRUCTURE

Organise the code into:
- app.py — Dash app init, layout, run server
- callbacks/investigation.py — all callbacks for this page
- callbacks/genie.py — Genie Space API call logic
- components/sidebar.py — sidebar filter component
- components/reason_cards.py — the 4 reason breakdown cards
- components/driver_table.py — the DataTable component
- components/chat.py — the Genie chat panel
- assets/custom.css — all custom CSS overrides

Use environment variables for all Databricks credentials. Never hardcode tokens.

